// AGENCY OST — 13 · Kill Switch
// ACT II finale. One command ends the rogue process — and the legacy system
// with it. The Agency motif (0 2 4 6 · 7 4 2 0) is no longer a melody:
// it IS the bass riff, distorted, full of stops, doubled by sub. Harmonic
// minor's raised 7th (b#) twists the last turnaround. Then the switch.
//
// FORM (100 BPM · 1 cycle = 1 bar · 68 bars ≈ 2:43 · loops):
//   intro   8  e1  sub drone + bells recall track 1; the console waits
//   arm     8  e3  kick + the motif-riff enters low and filtered
//   strike  16 e5  full: riff, half-time gated snare, lead doubles the motif
//   doubt   8  e2  hard stop — pad and bells; the hand hovers
//   strike2 16 e5  full + choir dread; the decision
//   flip    4  eX  THE SWITCH — one sub hit, then ringing silence
//   outro   8  e1  the old machine's drone, one last motif bell. Done.
// hook: the motif-as-riff — arm/strike/strike2; bells carry it elsewhere.

setbpm(100);

